Z||000000||Monkeyman||01-16-2000||12:56 PM||||There is another virus going around called "Happy99.exe"!!!! I got this attached to an email.  I got it from a fellow forum member so I know that it can get around without anyones knowledge.  (There's no way he would have sent it intentionally.)  I think I caught it in time and didn't do any damage, but I thought it might be wise to inform everyone since I send a fair amount of emails.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||01-16-2000||02:25 PM||||As long as you didn't open the exe file and see the fireworks you're OK. There are fixes for it on the net. Some one gave it to me last year. It attaches itself to all of your e-mail ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||01-16-2000||02:46 PM||||I work at Gateway, and we see it fairly frequently.  If you know you have it, do a search for ska.* and delete what if finds.  Then you can re-extract winsock.dll and wsock32.dll through system file checker.  There may be one more, but it's been awhile. You can extract these through system file checker in win98. On 95 is a b*tch cuz you gotta do it manually.  mcafee.com has some good detailed info on this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||01-16-2000||03:27 PM||||I've got that a couple times before.. I knew it was a virus tho, so I deleted the emails and told the person they were infected.<P>I'm also running the latest version of McAfee, so I'm not too worried. I do recommend that everyone get a current virus scanner and routinely check your files. Virii are getting "smarter", and harder to detect.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaRkLoRD||01-16-2000||03:32 PM||||I don't mean existing ones are, I mean the newer ones are getting better.. able to hide, move across networks, and execute themselves without the user running an EXE file. (thanks to the wonders of activex and other stuff like that which can be embedded into emails...)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||01-16-2000||04:05 PM||||Monkey,<BR> You didn't get it from me, did you?  I can't belive that virus is still going around!||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||01-16-2000||04:25 PM||||I got it from Monkey and deleted it, then told him. He said he got it from me a few days ago. My Norton Anti-Virus can't find any virus on my end. I tried searching for files called ska.* like bastard says, but it comes up blank. I "replied to author" via email with Monkey, so I bet he sent it to me and I sent it right back to him again and then he sent it back to me again. Nasty little computer bugs. We went through this at work too just recently.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||01-16-2000||05:08 PM||||Happy 99 has been around for some time. you either need to upgrade your antivirus, or you need to change to another program. McAfee virus scan has e-mail scanning. <P>Happy 99 is a macro trojan. It mails itself, usually as a second e-mail, every time you mail something. The trojan portion can only damage your system if you open it.<P>If you have your e-mail program set to preview mail, turn off preview(Both "preview pane" and the summary below the subject.) There are other e-mail bugs that execute even if all you do is preview. Those bugs contain either ActiveX(OCX) functions or VB scripts. Both OCX and VB script are free to do anything they want to your machine, unlike 'normal' JAVA functions which are not allowed to do things like format a hard drive.||||reg||1
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||01-16-2000||06:13 PM||||Monkey, you sent me an e-mail the other day. When it comes to computers, I am not very famaliar with them, I just usually play games and look up Fieros on the web and come here. So Monkey, since you knocked me up tell me how to get rid of it! I have an AMD 333 running 98 with no virus thingy.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||01-16-2000||06:27 PM||||I don't know who got it first.  The 1st time I saw it was with a batch of emails from batboy, but I guess that doesn't mean that I didn't give it to him 1st.  If I did, I had no idea.  Sorry!  Unfortunately, I did open it.  When I get emails, I usually see what the attachments are if they are from someone I know.  I remember that I got a couple that day from batboy (I'm not blaming you-just stating what happened!) and this one said it was from him, too.  I clicked on the paperclip and opened it directly so I saw the fireworks.  Then I saved it to my disc.  I never opened it again once I saved it to my disc though.  My virus checker program is out of date or old or something.  Maybe I've just used up my free time with it.  What will this do to my files and/or system? I'll start deleting stuff tonight like GT Bastard said if I can figure out exactly what he's talking about.  I don't know alot about computers so I'm a little unclear about that.  Hopefully I can fix it before it does any damage.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||01-16-2000||08:49 PM||||Guys--I don't know who got it first but if it was me I apologize from the bottom of my heart!  I feel really bad about this.  This is my 1st dealing with a virus (although I've heard of them before) and had no idea that I had one until batboy was so kind as to inform me.  I think I've made the fix, but just to be sure I've emailed GT Bastard.  He seems to know exactly what's going on and I don't think anyone can get it if they don't try to see the attachment.  Like I said, GT Bastard seems to know what to look for so I tried him.  If my email comes up clean with him and he tells me that I've done the right fixes, I'll be back.  If not and I've infected him, too, I'll just leave quietly.  For those of you who I've apparently infected, I'm truly sorry.  I'm still not sure exactly what can happen if this stupid thing runs rampant in your computer, but I'd hate to feel like I messed anyones system up.  Until you here from me again on the forum, don't feel like I'm ignoring you if I don't respond to your emails.  I just don't want this to happen again.<P>Until I'm fixed...||||reg||1
Z||000011||SCCA FIERO||01-16-2000||10:02 PM||||Monkey, I don't know if I even have it. I am not trying to make you feel bad or nutin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'm sure you wouldn't have gave it to me on purpose. Even if I have it and it destroys my computer I won't hold a grudge... like I said I know you didn't (if you did) want to spread it.<P>GT Bastard, how do I locate this thing if it's in my computer and how do I get rid of it? I did a search for "ska.*" and found nothing and also searched for "Happy99.exe" and found nothing. Maybe I didn't get it?<P>Again Monkey, don't sweat it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||01-17-2000||12:37 AM||||Happy99 is an annoyance, but it doesn't do any harm as far as I know.<P>Now.. W95.CIH... now there's a nasty virus. also known as Chernobyl.. I got it last year and I lost 400 megs of data, and was without my files for a month. I managed to recover everything except my primary partition (400 megs) but I had some clients who weren't too happy that I wasn't able to do any work on their sites for a month. Missed some school stuff too.. now I back up to a separate machine several times a day.. soon I'll have a firewall as well.||||reg||1
Z||000013||batboy||01-17-2000||12:44 AM||||Actually, most computer viruses are more annoying than harmful. Monkey, don't worry about it. You can't track these things down. It don't matter who got it first and accidently passed it along. Viruses are made to be sneaky like that. If this is your first, it won't be your last. We've dealt with a number of viruses at work over the last 3 years or so. We've never had a fatal crash yet. I've been very fortunate at home so far. I'm using the same Norton Anti-Virus 5.0 as what we have at work (Coincidence? I think not!) and Norton found the Happy99 bug on a co-worker's computer. My computer is clean and has been for a year. I do regular live anti-virus updates and weekly virus scans, plus I have the auto-protect mode enabled. Let's get paranoid, cause the bugs are out to get ya!||||reg||1
Z||000014||dogtired||01-17-2000||08:20 AM||||What do you all use to check out your systems???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>If it came from me "I am really SORRY" But if it did I still don't know I have it!!!<P>HELP<P>HELP <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000015||batboy||01-17-2000||09:49 AM||||The two best anti-virus programs right now are McAffe's and Norton's. Both allow you to hook in to their website for a periodic "live update" which adds the newest virus signatures to the program's database. Highly recommended.||||reg||1
Z||000016||GT Bastard||01-18-2000||03:05 AM||||Happy 99 CAN affect your computer.  It infects the "sock" files which are necessary for internet access.  Happy 99 alters, or "infects" the sock files and also creates a file called ska.dll  There might be another, but I'm too lazy to look it up.  There ARE different variations of it from what i've heard, but everyone that I've helped fix it over the phone with(at work) was unable to get on the internet or check email.  If you wanna get the best info on it, check Mcafee's website like Monkey did.  ||||reg||1
